title: Loom
text: Seven threads go into the loom. None is cut and none changes colour, and they still leave in a different order. A thread never turns on its own.
trick: a dual reflector at a crossing turns both beams at once, one on each face, so each carries on along the other's line: a swap. The exit colours are a permutation, and the solution is a twill: a staircase of swaps
motif: pictogram (a loom: warp and weft lanes in a wall field)
expect: shared>=5
---
L 0 4 2 b
L 0 7 2 m
L 0 10 2 r
L 3 14 0 y
L 6 14 0 g
L 9 14 0 w
L 12 14 0 c
*r 9 4 1 k
*r 12 4 1 k
*r 6 7 1 k
*r 9 7 1 k
*r 3 10 1 k
*r 6 10 1 k
T 14 4 0 ?
T 14 7 0 ?
T 14 10 0 ?
T 3 0 0 ?
T 6 0 0 ?
T 9 0 0 ?
T 12 0 0 ?
% walls: everything but the warp and weft
